From b56ae8129ae1be201555627519739b47a367310c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:23:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/56] Agent: per-beat checksums, command-stream report and
 poison diagnostics

For checking that a bridge game replays identically:

- every step message carries "beat" and "sums": the sim's own desync
  checksums (Sim::mSimHashes) of every beat finished since the previous
  message. /agentchecksum <n> sets sim_ChecksumPeriod for the session
  (stock 50; 1 checksums every beat).
- "stream" lists what the command stream carried besides beat
  bookkeeping ([beat, op, first payload byte]), so input that did not
  come from the agent -- e.g. the local UI issuing orders or sim
  callbacks for the agent's army -- shows up with the beat it landed in.
  CDecoder::DecodeMessage reports each message (AGENT_NoteStreamOp).
- /agentpoison <byte> fills every new heap block with the byte (through
  the allocator's memory hook) and scrubs 48 KB of the sim thread's stack
  around each beat and agent step. A read of uninitialised memory then
  gives the same value in every run, and two runs with different bytes
  split where such a read reaches the sim. /agentpoisonsizes <min> <max>
  and /agentpoisonbytes <from> <to> narrow the fill down, for bisecting
  the allocation and field (how the guard-scan read was found).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c464789609cee98601a7ad6f5c14402556e15998)
